  {"type": "split", "h2": "Heat pump installation in Huntsville with backup heat built in", "photo": "in", "reverse": True,
   "html": "<p>A heat pump's rating tells you the coldest temperature it can still produce heat at. Our Midea EVOX G3 and Kepler units carry a -30°C heating rating. In northern Muskoka, some winters bring nights near or past that, so a rating alone isn't a plan.</p>"
           "<p>The plan is a heat pump sized to carry most of the season, plus a backup sized to carry the whole house if it has to. In a home with a good furnace, the furnace becomes the backup. In an all-electric home, an electric air handler with heat strips does the job. Either way, the switch happens on its own and you stay warm.</p>"
           "<p>Bunkies and additions are simpler. A single-zone ductless system handles one space, and the main house's system doesn't have to change at all.</p>"
           "<ul class=\"checklist\"><li>Output checked at your design temperature, not just the label</li><li>A second heat source sized for the full load</li><li>Separate ductless zones for bunkies and additions</li><li>A clear path for defrost water, so no ice block forms below</li></ul>"},
